# ── Layout ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   game/    EXACTLY what deploys. Upload this folder and nothing else.
#   source/  authoring originals (.glb sculpts, the music library). NOT shipped,
#            and mostly NOT tracked — see below. Back this up separately.
#   tools/   the voxelisers, bakers and build scripts.
#   docs/    plans and notes.
#   engine/  THE engine: the voxel forest, path traced on Falcor.
#   launcher/  the self-extracting launcher that becomes voxelbit.exe.
#   dist/    what package.py builds. Never committed -- see below.
#
# 2026-09-06: v4, v5, v6 and the old OptiX v2 were deleted, and the Falcor
# engine that had been v7 took the name v2.
# 2026-09-21: the BROWSER engine was retired -- src/ and game/index.html are
# gone -- and the Falcor engine is simply the engine now.
# One launcher, run.bat, and one shipped artifact, voxelbit.exe. Nothing
# here names an engine that no longer exists.
#
# git here is for the CODE and the RUNTIME assets that make it run. Source art is
# binary, effectively static, does not need per-line history, and makes every git
# command crawl.
#
# 2026-07-18: game assets and sfx ARE tracked. They were ignored once, so a GitHub
# zip arrived with no models and no sound and the game could not run. Keep them in.
#
# 2026-07-24: site flattened, then restructured into game/ + source/ + tools/.
# The unused music libraries moved to source/audio/ and the .glb sculpts belong in
# source/glb/ — both excluded here. sound/sfx/ lives in game/ and stays TRACKED:
# it is the only audio index.html loads, and excluding it reintroduces the silent-
# game bug above.

# ── source art: large, binary, backed up outside git ──
# palm_tree.glb alone is 233 MB — over GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit, which
# would make the push fail outright. The audio library is ~646 MB and unreferenced.
source/glb/
source/audio/
# 2026-08-18: the .fbx sculpts + their textures, 32 MB. Same rule as source/glb/ above — authoring
# originals, not runtime assets. (A trailing `#` comment does NOT work here: git only treats `#` as a
# comment at the START of a line, so `source/fbx/  # note` is a literal pattern that matches nothing.)
source/fbx/
*.glb

# NOTE: source/wip/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It is work-in-progress voxel art
# kept out of game/ so it never deploys, but still tracked so it has a backup.

# ── legacy / scratch ──
# tools/frames/ is the frame-capture dump the video export writes (snap<timestamp> (NNNN).png).
# 120 stills of one clip is ~29 MB and it regenerates on demand — same reasoning as _snapshots/.
tools/frames/
# serve-nocache.py imports tools/bundle.py, so Python writes bytecode next to it
tools/__pycache__/
art/
.vox/
website_old/
_snapshots/
*.bak
*.log
node_modules/

# floatshots/ is the float-audit screenshot dump (__vb.floatAudit runs). 46 MB of
# regenerable test stills — same reasoning as tools/frames/ and _snapshots/ above.
floatshots/

# 2026-08-31: the NINE PINES. What ships is game/assets/foilage/pine9/*.vox (about 1 MB, fetched by
# assets/palette.js at boot) and tools/voxelize_pine9.py that bakes them - both TRACKED, so a fresh
# clone still grows a forest. What is excluded is the authoring input it bakes FROM:
#   game/assets/foilage/pine_trees/  the EuropeanPine .obj/.fbx and Textures.zip - 149 MB, and the zip
#                                    alone is 133 MB, past GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit, so this
#                                    is not a preference: a commit containing it cannot be pushed.
#   source/pine9/                    the textures unpacked from that zip, plus the 2 MB bake JSON.
# It sits under game/ only because that is where it was dropped; nothing at runtime reads it.
game/assets/foilage/pine_trees/
source/pine9/

# 2026-09-03: the end card's ALPHA master. docs/end-alpha.mov is ProRes 4444 (yuva444p12le, 4K,
# 192 frames) - 88 MB, and it is an authoring intermediate, not a deliverable: the two exports made
# from it, end-alpha.webm (VP9, alpha_mode=1) and end-alpha-matte.mp4 (the luma matte for NLEs that
# will not read alpha), are 3.5 MB together and ARE tracked. Same rule as source/glb/ above; it also
# sits close enough to GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit that a re-render could push a commit over.
docs/end-alpha.mov
renders/
v2_shot_*.png

# ── 2026-09-06: build output and scratch that must not reach GitHub ───────────
q.png
# Video captures written by the in-engine recorder. Output, not input.
v2_take_*.mp4
*.mp4

# Terrain data built by engine/tools/dem2raw.cpp and engine/tools/naip2cov.py.
# DERIVED, and large: a 60 km window is 130 MB, which is past GitHub's
# 100 MB hard limit and would have the push refused outright. Both files
# are rebuilt from the USGS tiles in minutes -- see engine/assets/dem/README.md.
engine/assets/dem/*.vbdem
engine/assets/dem/*.vbcov

# Built by hand from tools/*.cpp; not a deliverable.
engine/tools/*.exe

# ── 2026-09-21: the shipped build ────────────────────────────────────────────
# tools/package.py lays a 1.4 GB staging tree into dist/stage and compresses it
# into voxelbit.exe AT THE ROOT, beside the run script, where a player expects
# to double-click it. Both are DERIVED from this repository in a couple of
# minutes and both are far past GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit, so a commit
# that caught either would simply be refused -- after uploading most of a
# gigabyte first. Ship the exe from a release, not from the tree.
dist/
/voxelbit.exe
# ...AND THE COPY STAGED FOR UPLOAD. The rule above is anchored to the root, so
# the 522 MB installer the website folder carries for deploy was not covered by
# it -- and GitHub hard-rejects any single file over 100 MB, so this is a push
# that fails rather than a repo that grows. website/ itself is SOURCE and is
# tracked; only the artifact is not.
website/voxelbit.exe

# The launcher's own build output. launcher.cpp and launcher/build.bat are the
# source and ARE tracked; the exe, the object and the compiled icon are not.
launcher/launcher.exe
launcher/*.obj
launcher/*.res
launcher/icon.rc

# The crash reports the engine writes beside itself -- see engine/src/platform/
# crashlog.h. They are evidence from one run on one machine, and a .dmp is
# tens of megabytes. Attach one to an issue; do not commit it.
v2-crash.log
v2-crash-*.dmp

# Scratch backups taken before a destructive asset regeneration. The originals
# they hold are the committed versions of the same files, so git already has
# them and a second copy is only noise in the tree.
game/assets/**/_pre-revoxel-*/

# MagicaVoxel's own settings, dropped here because the editor gets run from
# this directory. Its fonts, its .ui layouts and a workspace full of absolute
# paths off one machine -- nothing in this project reads any of it.
/config/
